{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Statute and ordinance</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the other two as in Joshua: \"and he set them statute and ordinance\" (בשכם) — as when he cut a covenant with Israel. And the other: \"and to teach in Israel statute and ordinance\" — in Ezra. As there, statutes and ordinances were given to them, so too in Joshua it is as though the Torah was given to them on that very day, for they accepted to serve YHWH; and so too in Ezra the script of the Torah was renewed for them." "<b>There He set for him statute and ordinance</b> This is the red heifer: just as this [tree] — the bitter — sweetens the bitter waters, so the red heifer purifies the impure and impurifies the pure." "<b>There</b> in gematria: פרה אדומה (red heifer)."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:08.360615284Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}